  "text": "Question nine. Sketch a fraud detection ML system. Features first: the amount, the merchant category, time since the last transaction, device and location, and velocity, the card's transactions in the last hour and the last day. The model is gradient boosting, which suits tabular data like this, or a neural network over the card's history. It runs online, at authorization, in under a hundred milliseconds, so the velocity counts come from the online store. Its threshold is set by cost: a missed fraud against a good customer declined. Labels are chargebacks, confirmed fraud, and they arrive late. So train only on transactions old enough for their chargebacks to have landed, or fresh fraud is learned as honest. Then monitor precision and recall as the labels arrive, and drift in the velocity features before they do.",
